                    {
                        "form_id": "0d986611-e369-4a00-ab7b-19e5dc74ff7a",
                        "entry_id": "ef3a260f-dc2e-315c-bf42-0aa0d50f721a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "жнеца́х"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0bfd8eaf-2d34-3966-8c34-8e4eb2c33fb4",
                        "entry_id": "ef3a260f-dc2e-315c-bf42-0aa0d50f721a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "тот, кто жнёт хлебные злаки"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4979e958-f904-45e3-9657-8e22baefe89b",
                                "sense_id": "0bfd8eaf-2d34-3966-8c34-8e4eb2c33fb4",
                                "text": "Афанасий Иванович очень мало занимался хозяйством, хотя впрочем ездил иногда к косарям и жнецам и смотрел довольно пристально на их работу; всё бремя правления лежало на Пульхерии Ивановне."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd606ae7-6a58-4f2e-83d6-cf1c2a484417",
                                "sense_id": "0bfd8eaf-2d34-3966-8c34-8e4eb2c33fb4",
                                "text": "Такое существо, которое пока растет, так ничего в нем нет, а вырастет, станет ни швец, ни жнец, ни в дуду игрец."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e993a29e-b04e-4322-950f-68c28e79ccf2",
                                "sense_id": "0bfd8eaf-2d34-3966-8c34-8e4eb2c33fb4",
                                "text": "Не хватало рук для жатвы: соседний однодворец, с самым благообразным лицом, порядился доставить жнецов по два рубля с десятины и надул самым бессовестным образом; свои бабы заламывали цены неслыханные, а хлеб между тем осыпался, а тут с косьбой не совладели, а тут Опекунский совет грозится и требует немедленной и безнедоимочной уплаты процентов…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e84c8c75-3c50-4abb-9dd3-14c29715c889",
                        "source_entry_id": "ef3a260f-dc2e-315c-bf42-0aa0d50f721a",
                        "source_sense_id": "0bfd8eaf-2d34-3966-8c34-8e4eb2c33fb4",
                        "target_lang_word": "reaper",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "reaper",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "279aa8ac-87b3-3ec3-aa99-3418adea458f",
                                        "entry_id": "bdf1e0f7-3ea2-3c8e-8c69-219b086fc319",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who reaps; a person employed to harvest crops from the fields by reaping."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a78ba795-ff0f-4302-9814-7b273c8a0b68",
                                                "sense_id": "279aa8ac-87b3-3ec3-aa99-3418adea458f",
                                                "text": "Even as we looked some rumour seemed to have spread, for we saw the reapers hurrying from the fields."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "087c5f6a-544e-3546-bc93-3e98d6bf7cea",
                                        "entry_id": "bdf1e0f7-3ea2-3c8e-8c69-219b086fc319",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A machine used to harvest crops."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "72a8ee8a-311f-3c38-a18e-12406445fd60",
                                        "entry_id": "bdf1e0f7-3ea2-3c8e-8c69-219b086fc319",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of Grim Reaper."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "capitalized",
                                            "ellipsis",
                                            "often"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ded91f44-a435-40b8-94a7-276829636023",
                                                "sense_id": "72a8ee8a-311f-3c38-a18e-12406445fd60",
                                                "text": "Thereafter when their cups were brimmed anew with foaming wine the Red Foliot spake among them and said, “O ye lords of Witchland, will you that I speak a dirge in honour of Gorice the King that the dark reaper hath this day gathered?”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1fea9ab-f47c-49ab-9226-bfc4538c2bc7",
                                                "sense_id": "72a8ee8a-311f-3c38-a18e-12406445fd60",
                                                "text": "Don't fear the Reaper / We'll be able to fly"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8dbeb545-a7e0-4fce-bbfe-eb29b9dca99b",
                                                "sense_id": "72a8ee8a-311f-3c38-a18e-12406445fd60",
                                                "text": "Why is the Grim Reaper a man? True, the noun ending would theoretically allow us to visualize the reaper as a woman as well, but we don't."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07eeca31-26d5-4006-8157-abb4e0acb419",
                                                "sense_id": "72a8ee8a-311f-3c38-a18e-12406445fd60",
                                                "text": "She told me she wanted to meet the reaper\nI had only done her a favor\nShe didn't deserve to die\nBut I deserved to kill her"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e491bddf-88fb-3530-a746-4c1aa4409261",
                                        "entry_id": "bdf1e0f7-3ea2-3c8e-8c69-219b086fc319",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A recluse spider (Loxosceles and Sicarius spp.)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
